 <notes>
    - New: opt-in function source map. With xhprof.collect_files=1 the
      extension records the file and declaration line of every profiled
      user function (functions, methods and closures; internals and the
      load::/eval:: entries carry no file of their own). The map travels
      with the run file as "__files__"; the reporting layer strips it on
      read (get_run() output is unchanged, get_run_files() serves it),
      shows "file:line" next to the function name in the flat,
      parent-child and single-function views, and exports it under
      "files" in format=json. Runs profiled without the setting simply
      have no map and no extra UI.
    - The setting defaults to 0: while enabled, each profiled call pays
      one hash lookup to remember the file - measured at ~30ns per call
      (+11% on top of the profiler's own overhead in a tight call loop);
      a run file grows by the map, ~100 bytes per distinct function.
    - New extension test xhprof_026.phpt covers the collection, the
      recursion/base-name keying and the opt-in behavior; the extension
      suite passes 26/26 and the report-layer suite 156/156 on PHP 8.5.
    - Everything else is identical to 2.3.15.
 </notes>
